<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE pkgmetadata SYSTEM "http://www.gentoo.org/dtd/metadata.dtd">
<pkgmetadata>
  <maintainer type="person">
    <!-- Ebuild on the oiledmachine-overlay -->
    <email>orsonteodoro@hotmail.com</email>
    <name>Orson Teodoro</name>
  </maintainer>
  <!--

    oiledmachine-overlay notes:

    The amdgpu-drm is a virtual ebuild.   It was originally intended as a way
    to choose either between the amdgpu driver in the amdgpu-dkms package or the
    amdgpu driver provided by the kernel package.[1]

    Historically, it used the DC_VER from the amdgpu-dkms package as a way to
    ensure correspondence and equivalence between the ROCm version and DC_VER in
    both the vanilla kernel and the ROCK-Kernel-Driver.  The flaw in the
    assumption has been corrected.

    To find the vanilla kernel equivalent, we see the most recent last commits of

      https://github.com/ROCm/ROCK-Kernel-Driver/commits/rocm-@ROCM_VERSION@/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd

    are present in the vanilla kernel.

    | KFD ABI [3]  | DC [3]  | GC [3] | VCN [3] | ROCm version [3] | Vanilla kernel only equivalent   | amdgpu-dkms supported kernel versions [4]  |
    |--------------|---------|--------|---------|------------------|----------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
    | 1.17         | 3.2.319 | 12.0.1 | 5.0.1   | 6.4.0            | 6.15                             | 4.18 - 6.11, <= 6.12.x                     |
    | 1.17         | 3.2.320 | 12.0.1 | 5.0.1   | 6.4.3            | 6.15                             | 4.18 - 6.11, <= 6.12.x                     |
    | 1.18         | 3.2.339 | 12.0.1 | 5.0.1   | 7.0.2            | 6.17                             | 4.18 - 6.14, <= 6.14.x                     |
    | 1.18         | 3.2.351 | 12.0.1 | 5.0.1   | 7.1.1            | 6.18                             | 4.18 - 6.14, <= 6.16.x                     |
    | 1.18         | 3.2.359 | 12.0.1 | 5.0.1   | 7.2.4            | 6.19                             | 4.18 - 6.14, <= 6.16.x                     |
    | 1.23         | 3.2.384 | 12.1.0 | 5.3.0   | live             | live                             | <= 6.19.x                                  |

    The userspace packages rely on GC for compute and VCN for GPU video decoding.

    Terms/purpose according to AI:

     GC - contains the compute units
     DC - driver architecture
    DCN - handles output timing, composting
    KFD - queue management
    PSP - trusted execution, secure firmware loading
    VCN - hardare decoding

    Footnotes:

    [1]  Verified claim:  https://github.com/ROCm/ROCm/blob/rocm-4.5.2/README.md#rocm-support-in-upstream-linux-kernels
    [2]  Version constraints or version contract:  https://github.com/ROCm/rocm-install-on-linux/blob/rocm-7.2.0/docs/reference/user-kernel-space-compat-matrix.rst
    [3]  Based on https://github.com/ROCm/amdgpu repo
    [4]  Partly based on https://github.com/ROCm/rocm-install-on-linux/blob/rocm-7.2.0/docs/reference/system-requirements.rst tables left side, right side is based on Makefile in [3].

  -->
  <use>
    <flag name="amdgpu-dkms">
      Selects amdgpu-dkms as a DRM module driver.

      (Recommended for feature completeness and kernel configuration
      correctness.)
    </flag>
    <flag name="amdgpu-dkms-firmware">
      Select the amdgpu-dkms-firmware package as the firmware source.
    </flag>
    <flag name="custom-kernel">
      Disable *DEPENDs checks.
    </flag>
    <flag name="linux-firmware">
      Select the linux-firmware package as the firmware source.
    </flag>
    <flag name="kernel">
      Selects the in kernel sources which will contain the amdgpu DRM driver.

      (Recommended for minimal install and better security, but you are
      responsible for the proper kernel configuration.)
    </flag>
    <flag name="strict-pairing">
      Both the firmware and DRM driver are paired so the kernel driver
      corresponding to ROCm 5.1.3 matches the corresponding the ROCm 5.1.3
      firmware.  Otherwise, the kernel driver is paired greater than or equal to
      the firmware release.
    </flag>
  </use>
</pkgmetadata>
